go 1.25.0

// The CLI and the command sets that bundled plugins contribute to it.
//
// Go has no usable dynamic plugin loading for a single static binary
// (`plugin.Open` demands an identical toolchain and identical versions of
// every shared dependency, and does not support Windows), so a plugin's
// commands are compiled in from its own module here instead. `plugins/*/cli`
// is where a plugin owns its CLI surface, which keeps it deletable with the
// rest of the plugin.
//
// The module graph is intentionally cyclic -- the CLI imports the plugin to
// register its commands, the plugin imports cli/pkg/api to talk to the
// instance. Go allows that; only the *package* graph has to be acyclic, and
// it is.
use ./cli
use ./plugins/scheduled_tasks/cli
